    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.152.1

Upstream patch release: Guardian approval review now sources its Node
REPL policy from model metadata, and a mid-session model switch is
refused when the destination changes that policy.

Vendored crate set is byte-identical to 0.152.0 (same 1192 crates);
upstream changed 12 files and the only manifest change is the
workspace version stamp, so License: and the Legal-Review-Notice
counts stand.  Re-derived anyway: 875 linked crates on aarch64 = 748
third-party + 127 first-party.  Both downstream patches re-verified at
--fuzz=0.  cargo-audit on a bare Cargo.lock reports the same five
advisories as 0.152.0, already documented in _service and the 0.152.0
changelog entry.

Built locally on aarch64 and on OBS for x86_64 and aarch64: rpmlint 0
errors / 0 warnings / 0 badness, %check 763 tests, 0 failed.</comment>
